# Assistive calling project rules

Negotiator is being converted into an assistive calling app. A person who cannot speak types text to be spoken on a real phone call, reads live captions, and approves AI-drafted replies.

- Never log transcripts, phone numbers, or personal data. Log only IDs and event types.
- All secrets come from environment variables. Keep `.env.example` up to date. Never commit secrets.
- Every API route must check the authenticated user and call ownership.
- Validate all external input with zod.
- Twilio webhooks must be signature-verified.
- Nothing AI-written is spoken on a call until the user approves it (except in the future Delegated mode).
- Accessibility first: large touch targets, labels on every control, screen reader friendly, no microphone required.
- Make small, reviewable changes and list the files touched at the end of each task.
